  "reconstructionNotes": "Lay out left-to-right on a white background: single neutron → large spherical U-235 cluster → arrow → vertically elongated, waist-pinched U-236 cluster with a thin red outline and 'Unstable nucleus' caption → two diverging arrows → upper-right Kr-92 cluster and lower-right Ba-141 cluster, with a gold multi-point starburst labeled 'Energy' between them and three small neutron spheres with arrows at the far right. Render nucleons as two alternating sphere colors (medium green ~#7cb342 and off-white/light gray ~#e0e0d8) with soft shading so clusters read as 3D ball packs. Place the full balanced equation in black along the bottom with rightward arrows between each stage. For the chain-reaction slider, draw a small branching tree (1 node → 3 → 9 → 27) that grows with the slider value, reusing the same neutron/cluster glyphs; keep the main fission scene static while the tree animates so the two views do not compete."
