userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: Absorbing a single slow neutron makes U-235 briefly form an unstable U-236 that splits into two lighter nuclei plus three new neutrons and a large energy burst, so one fission can trigger several more — the basis of a self-sustaining chain reaction.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): One neutron in produces three neutrons out, so fission events multiply generation by generation — that neutron surplus, not just the energy release, is what allows a self-sustaining chain reaction.
DEMO STEPS: 5 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

